{"uid":"dc3f7e08d63a89ff","name":"Every row carries the tenant of its owner [deliveries]","fullName":"tests.db_tests.test_storage_facts#test_every_row_carries_the_tenant_of_its_owner","historyId":"0689e6fcb11c686e78b708cdf7f629cc","time":{"start":1787469451443,"stop":1787469451472,"duration":29},"description":"The API cannot see this: none of these three tables is reachable over HTTP\nwith its `tenant_id` attached.\n\n`DeliveryOut` has no `tenant_id` field at all, and `webhook_events` and\n`notification_impressions` have no endpoint whatsoever. So a row could be\nwritten under the wrong tenant and every HTTP test in this suite would still\npass — the mis-stamped row would simply be invisible until it surfaced as one\norganisation's analytics quietly counting another's sends.\n\nTenant isolation is tested over HTTP as a *permission* — acme asks for\nglobex's record and is told it does not exist. This is the same promise as a\n*storage* fact: the data was filed under the right owner in the first place.\nA system can pass the first and fail the second, and the failure is the worse\nof the two because nothing reports it.\n","descriptionHtml":"<p>The API cannot see this: none of these three tables is reachable over HTTP<br />\nwith its <code>tenant_id</code> attached.</p>\n<p><code>DeliveryOut</code> has no <code>tenant_id</code> field at all, and <code>webhook_events</code> and<br />\n<code>notification_impressions</code> have no endpoint whatsoever. So a row could be<br />\nwritten under the wrong tenant and every HTTP test in this suite would still<br />\npass — the mis-stamped row would simply be invisible until it surfaced as one<br />\norganisation's analytics quietly counting another's sends.</p>\n<p>Tenant isolation is tested over HTTP as a <em>permission</em> — acme asks for<br />\nglobex's record and is told it does not exist. This is the same promise as a<br />\n<em>storage</em> fact: the data was filed under the right owner in the first place.<br />\nA system can pass the first and fail the second, and the failure is the worse<br />\nof the two because nothing reports it.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"base_url","time":{"start":1787469442719,"stop":1787469442719,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"delete_output_dir","time":{"start":1787469442720,"stop":1787469442720,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_verify_url","time":{"start":1787469442720,"stop":1787469442720,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"settings","time":{"start":1787469442720,"stop":1787469442721,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"pytestconfig","time":{"start":1787469442720,"stop":1787469442720,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"database_state","time":{"start":1787469442722,"stop":1787469444766,"duration":2044},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1787469442722,"stop":1787469442722,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":fals